 "text": "Births in World 1950-2026 & Future Projections | database.earth\n\n# Population Births in World\n\nIn 2025, 132,399,173 people was born in World. That is a -0.01% decrease of births when compared to previous year. This number is set to increase by 104296 births in 2026, when the total birth count for the year, is project to be 132,503,469.\n\n## Historic Birth Count in World (1950-2025)\n\nWorld has seen an increase of births since the 1950's. From 91,823,936 to 132,399,173 yearly births, a total increase of 44.19%.\n\n Date Source: UN World Population Prospects (2024) | License: CCBY | Note: Values indicate mid year (1 July)\n\n| Year | Births |\n| --- | --- |\n| 1950 | 91,823,936 |\n| 1951 | 92,507,128 |\n| 1952 | 97,371,459 |\n| 1953 | 97,291,452 |\n| 1954 | 100,187,854 |\n| 1955 | 101,747,972 |\n| 1956 | 101,759,013 |\n| 1957 | 106,017,733 |\n| 1958 | 104,644,163 |\n| 1959 | 101,999,844 |\n| 1960 | 102,378,083 |\n| 1961 | 100,950,944 |\n| 1962 | 112,038,714 |\n| 1963 | 119,802,888 |\n| 1964 | 117,292,200 |\n| 1965 | 117,837,004 |\n| 1966 | 117,232,950 |\n| 1967 | 116,920,266 |\n| 1968 | 121,825,890 |\n| 1969 | 122,227,965 |\n| 1970 | 124,135,907 |\n| 1971 | 123,739,681 |\n| 1972 | 123,554,018 |\n| 1973 | 123,563,931 |\n| 1974 | 122,709,409 |\n| 1975 | 121,030,095 |\n| 1976 | 121,322,351 |\n| 1977 | 120,786,521 |\n| 1978 | 122,140,645 |\n| 1979 | 125,000,293 |\n| 1980 | 127,446,984 |\n| 1981 | 129,715,837 |\n| 1982 | 133,206,504 |\n| 1983 | 131,967,708 |\n| 1984 | 134,365,258 |\n| 1985 | 136,373,957 |\n| 1986 | 139,301,162 |\n| 1987 | 141,346,561 |\n| 1988 | 140,985,956 |\n| 1989 | 142,249,031 |\n| 1990 | 143,461,425 |\n| 1991 | 138,306,865 |\n| 1992 | 136,591,255 |\n| 1993 | 135,632,145 |\n| 1994 | 135,142,908 |\n| 1995 | 134,850,043 |\n| 1996 | 134,321,023 |\n| 1997 | 133,985,669 |\n| 1998 | 133,857,525 |\n| 1999 | 134,058,675 |\n| 2000 | 135,758,482 |\n| 2001 | 135,379,993 |\n| 2002 | 135,396,478 |\n| 2003 | 135,700,801 |\n| 2004 | 136,596,328 |\n| 2005 | 137,166,462 |\n| 2006 | 138,469,296 |\n| 2007 | 139,935,794 |\n| 2008 | 141,758,720 |\n| 2009 | 142,968,320 |\n| 2010 | 143,354,237 |\n| 2011 | 143,878,789 |\n| 2012 | 146,054,881 |\n| 2013 | 145,014,783 |\n| 2014 | 145,268,255 |\n| 2015 | 144,333,945 |\n| 2016 | 144,854,100 |\n| 2017 | 143,601,801 |\n| 2018 | 140,332,732 |\n| 2019 | 138,596,791 |\n| 2020 | 134,719,611 |\n| 2021 | 133,448,839 |\n| 2022 | 132,475,391 |\n| 2023 | 132,110,264 |\n| 2024 | 132,405,927 |\n| 2025 | 132,399,173 |\n\n## Birth Count Projections for 🏳️ World in 2026\n\n- In 2026, 132,503,469 babies will be born in World.\n- For every 1,000 children born in World, 138.1349 will succumb due to infant mortality.\n- This year, 104,296 more babies will be born in World when compared to previous year.\n\n## Future Births in World (2026-2100)\n\nWorld's negative trend in yearly birth count is not projected to continue into the future. The number of newborns per year will decrease from 132,503,469 to 110,028,472 between the year 2026 and 2100. A decrease of World's yearly birth count by -16.96% in 74 years.\n\n| Year | Births |\n| --- | --- |\n| 2026 | 132,503,469 |\n| 2027 | 132,590,971 |\n| 2028 | 132,761,183 |\n| 2029 | 132,988,654 |\n| 2030 | 133,256,397 |\n| 2031 | 133,513,402 |\n| 2032 | 133,764,794 |\n| 2033 | 134,065,211 |\n| 2034 | 134,381,002 |\n| 2035 | 134,669,241 |\n| 2036 | 134,945,606 |\n| 2037 | 135,140,994 |\n| 2038 | 135,355,315 |\n| 2039 | 135,515,309 |\n| 2040 | 135,668,984 |\n| 2041 | 135,672,675 |\n| 2042 | 135,635,914 |\n| 2043 | 135,580,927 |\n| 2044 | 135,406,650 |\n| 2045 | 135,108,935 |\n| 2046 | 134,763,860 |\n| 2047 | 134,270,884 |\n| 2048 | 133,752,123 |\n| 2049 | 133,163,337 |\n| 2050 | 132,555,180 |\n| 2051 | 131,922,869 |\n| 2052 | 131,280,338 |\n| 2053 | 130,666,632 |\n| 2054 | 130,019,574 |\n| 2055 | 129,484,557 |\n| 2056 | 128,994,835 |\n| 2057 | 128,530,513 |\n| 2058 | 128,109,976 |\n| 2059 | 127,754,769 |\n| 2060 | 127,431,153 |\n| 2061 | 127,116,967 |\n| 20